{"id": "tea:purusarthasiddhyupaya:177-178", "source": "src:purusarthasiddhyupaya", "location": {"ref": "177-178", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Since death is certain, one who, free of attachment and the like, acts only to thin the passions and the body does not kill himself; but one who, overcome by passion, ends his life by water, fire, poison or weapon, truly commits self-killing.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["death-dying", "ethics"], "terms": ["trm:sallekhana"], "concepts": ["cpt:sallekhana"], "teachers": ["tch:amrtacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "restricted": true, "notes": "Restricted: the text's own distinction. Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:purusarthasiddhyupaya:42", "source": "src:purusarthasiddhyupaya", "location": {"ref": "42", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Because they injure the soul's own states, falsehood and the rest are all violence; they are named separately only to instruct the disciple.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "terms": ["trm:himsa"], "concepts": ["cpt:ahimsa-jain"], "teachers": ["tch:amrtacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:purusarthasiddhyupaya:44", "source": "src:purusarthasiddhyupaya", "location": {"ref": "44", "section": null}, "original": {"text": "aprādurbhāvaḥ khalu rāgādīnāṃ bhavaty ahiṃseti / teṣām evotpattir hiṃseti jināgamasya saṃkṣepaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled by the unit author (wording believed standard; to be checked against an edition)", "licence": "public-domain text"}, "paraphrase": "The non-arising of attachment and the other [passions] is non-violence; their arising is violence — this is the essence of the Jina's teaching.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:ahimsa", "trm:himsa"], "concepts": ["cpt:ahimsa-jain"], "teachers": ["tch:amrtacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:purusarthasiddhyupaya:5", "source": "src:purusarthasiddhyupaya", "location": {"ref": "5", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The ultimate standpoint (niścaya) is described as the real (bhūtārtha), the conventional (vyavahāra) as the unreal (abhūtārtha).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:niscaya", "trm:vyavahara-naya", "trm:bhutartha", "trm:abhutartha"], "concepts": ["cpt:niscaya-vyavahara"], "teachers": ["tch:amrtacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
